    "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
    "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Escaped icons pass as names**\n\nThe naming lint accepts `BarIconButton { accessibleName: \"\\ue900\" }` even though its name is only an icon. `tokens()` keeps the escape as ASCII characters, so `glyph_string()` returns false and the name passes. This leaves screen reader users with an unreadable name despite a passing test.\n\nDecode QML Unicode escapes before checking glyphs, and add a",
    "automated": true,
    "task": "house-policy",
    "url": "https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy/pull/13212"
  },
  {
    "token": "review-comment:4308149471:2026-10-18T18:17:59Z:",
    "type": "review-comment",
    "source": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/13212#discussion_r4308149471",
    "head": "fbaecdd2aaf2f946c691ffd928ccb304aa32cdb7",
    "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
    "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Unnamed buttons pass the check**\n\nThe naming lint skips any `Button` whose explicit `text` is not a glyph, including `text: \"\"`. Thus `Button { iconText: \"\\ue900\"; text: \"\" }` passes without a name, even though `Button.accessibleName` resolves to an empty string. This leaves a gap in the check meant to catch unnamed controls for screen-reader users.\n\nOnly skip buttons with non-emp",
