    "head": "4c66862157bad42a3a71ebba1f1af2d6911c21b3",
    "author": "calebl",
    "body": "Agreed, `CursorSurface` should only report selection for rows that are a real choice. That means a `selectable` opt-in on the kit row, with each panel opting in its choice rows, which is a kit API change across first-party and third-party plugins. I'm leaving it for a separate follow-up so this PR stays focused on exposing the controls. `Button` already follows this rule here, and `ConfirmDialog`'s actions no longer report selection.\n",
